      "position": [
        1792,
        944
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1264,
        "height": 704,
        "content": "## Salesforce Sync\nThis section ensures that contract analysis results are stored and updated in Salesforce.\nChecks if the contract exists in Salesforce, creates a new record if needed, merges data, and updates the record with analysis results.\n\nThe contract record is updated with:\n   - Overall risk level\n   - Summary\n   - Top risks\n   - Recommendations\n\nThis guarantees that contract intelligence is persistently stored and kept up to date."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "80bbd548-028f-492a-8db7-ce48e106b297",
      "name": "Sticky Note6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3120,
        1120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 480,
        "height": 400,
        "content": "## Notification\nSends a Slack message with the final contract risk summary and key insights."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "abd44edc-5b37-4f3f-8a39-9f22e057f13b",
      "name": "Sticky Note7",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        16,
        400
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 896,
        "height": 1040,
        "content": "## \n### Summary\nThis workflow automates end-to-end contract analysis using AI. It monitors a Google Drive folder for new contract files, extracts and processes the document text, and uses large language models to identify key clauses, assess risks, and generate actionable insights.\n\nThe workflow produces a structured risk report containing overall risk level, summary, top risks, and recommendations. Results are stored in Salesforce for tracking and a summary notification is sent to Slack for visibility.\n\n### How It Works\n1. A new contract file is detected in a specified Google Drive folder.\n2. The file is validated (PDF only), downloaded, and its name is extracted.\n3. The PDF content is converted into clean text and split into smaller chunks.\n4. Each chunk is processed by an AI model to extract and classify contract clauses.\n5. Extracted clauses are analyzed to determine risk levels, issues, and recommendations.\n6. All analysis results are aggregated into a final contract risk report.\n7. The workflow checks if the contract exists in Salesforce:\n   - Creates a new record if not found\n   - Updates the existing record with analysis results\n8. A formatted summary is sent to Slack including risk level and key insights.\n### Setup Steps\n1. Connect Google Drive credentials and select the target folder.\n2. Configure Groq/OpenAI API credentials for all AI nodes.\n3. Connect Salesforce and ensure the custom object (Contract_AI__c) exists with required fields.\n4. Connect Slack and select the target channel.\n5. Verify field mappings (contract name, risk level, summary, etc.).\n6. Test the workflow with a sample PDF contract.\n7. Activate the workflow."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
